                <pb facs="1148" n="1028" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg1028"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Bowen to the Minister of Foreign
                        Affairs.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Caracas</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1905-03-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 19,
                    1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I have the honor to request your
                    excellency to inform me whether or not the Government of Venezuela will accept
                    the final proposal of arbitration which is contained in the accompanying copy of
                    instructions I received yesterday from Washington?</p>
                <p>I gladly avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Herbert W. Bowen</hi>.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
